{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310634,"nonce":"AUt26GQkN/GQqB4eS/50JfLp5Dk=","title":"FIXED — Int-bound enum-pattern variable assigned to a Float-typed temp in switch-as-expression desugar leaked i64 bits into f64 phi (no ...","message":"```haxe\nenum V { IntV(x:Int); FloatV(x:Float); }\nstatic function getFloat(v:V):Float {\n    return switch (v) {\n        case FloatV(x): x;\n        case IntV(x): x;  // \u003c-- Int x flowing into Float-typed switch\n    };\n}\ntrace(getFloat(IntV(100)));   // printed ~5e-322 (= i64 bit pattern 100 reinterpreted as f64)\n```\n\nSingle-arm switch (no FloatV branch) returned correct values via the\nReturn-handler coercion. Two-arm form went through the temp+phi desugar\nwhere the i64 register flowed into an f64 phi unconverted.\n\nReal-world surface: `nue.loader.GGUFLoader.readFloatOr` uses\n`case U32(x) | I32(x): x;` to widen integer GGUF metadata values into\nthe Float-returning function — same shape, same bug.\n\n\nSwitch-as-expression with constructor patterns desugars to:\n```\nvar _tmp:Float = 0.0;       // F64 register from init\nswitch (v) {\n    case FloatV(x): _tmp = x;   // x is F64 — fine\n    case IntV(x):   _tmp = x;   // x is I64 — needs sitofp before phi\n}\nreturn _tmp;\n```\n\nThe `HirStatement::Assign` handler in\n[compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs:4600+](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L4600)\ndid *not* insert an int→float cast when the lhs was a Float-typed\ntemp. Compounding factor: `gen_temp_var()` in\n[compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs:3740](compiler/src/ir/tast_to_hir.rs#L3740)\nmints a synthetic `SymbolId` but never registers it in `symbol_table`,\nso any attempt to look up the temp's TypeId returns invalid.\n\n\nIn the Assign handler's coercion block:\n1. First try `symbol_table.get(lhs_sym).type_id`.\n2. **Fall back** to `builder.get_register_type(symbol_map[lhs_sym])`\n   — the Let-init step set this to F64 when the desugar wrote\n   `_tmp = 0.0`.\n3. If lhs IR type is float and rhs IR type is int (or vice versa),\n   emit a `build_cast` (sitofp / fptosi).\n\nSame fix shape was already in the Return handler ([hir_to_mir.rs:5004](compiler/src/ir/hir_to_mir.rs#L5004)) for `return x;` patterns. This adds parity in Assign.\n\n\nWhenever a pattern-bound variable from an enum-variant field with a\nnarrower numeric type than the switch's unified result type leaks\ninto the result, the bug is now caught at the temp's Assign site.\nThis includes all `readFloatOr` / `metaFloat`-style helpers in nue\nthat use `case I32(x) | F32(x): x;`.\n\nThe deeper \"anon struct field scramble\" bug ([[bugs-anon-field-scramble]])\nis a *separate* defect not fixed by this — that one is positional\ntypedef field index mismatch, not a primitive promotion miss.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_int_float_assign_coerce` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}